---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DeptCalculator from '../components/DeptCalculator.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Sleep Debt Calculator | Track & Recover Lost Sleep';
const pageDescription =
    'Easily calculate your weekly sleep debt based on age. Get personalized tips to recover and improve your sleep quality. Free, fast, and accurate.';
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
    <DeptCalculator />

    <div class="container seo-content">
        <h2>Welcome to our Sleep Dept Calculator!</h2>
        <p>
            Getting enough sleep isn't just about how early you go to bed — it's
            about consistency and meeting your body's true needs. This simple
            tool helps you track your weekly sleep, calculate any sleep debt
            you've accumulated, and understand how it may be impacting your
            energy, mood, and focus. Whether you're trying to recover from a
            busy week or improve your long-term sleep habits, you're in the
            right place. Let's find out how much rest you really need.
        </p>

        <h2>What is Sleep Debt?</h2>
        <p>
            Sleep debt is the difference between the amount of sleep your body
            needs and the amount you actually get. Over time, even losing just a
            little sleep each night can add up—leading to fatigue, poor
            concentration, weakened immunity, and other health issues. Our Sleep
            Debt Calculator helps you track how much rest you're missing and
            gives you personalized tips on how to recover.
        </p>

        <h2>Why Track Your Sleep Debt?</h2>
        <p>
            Tracking sleep debt is an important step in building healthy sleep
            habits. Whether you're a teenager who needs more sleep than you
            realize or an adult juggling a busy schedule, being aware of your
            sleep patterns helps you make informed decisions about your bedtime,
            morning routine, and overall wellness.
        </p>

        <h2>How This Calculator Works</h2>
        <p>
            This tool uses your age range to determine your recommended nightly
            sleep duration and compares it to your actual sleep over the past
            week. The result includes your total sleep time, accumulated sleep
            debt, and practical suggestions based on your current sleep habits.
        </p>

        <p>
            If you're looking to plan your ideal bedtime based on a specific
            wake-up time, check out our <a href="/sleep-time-calculator/"
                >Sleep Time Calculator</a
            > — a great companion tool for improving your sleep routine.
        </p>

        <p>
            <strong>Tip:</strong> Try to go to bed and wake up at the same time every
            day, even on weekends. Consistency is key to healthy, restorative sleep.
        </p>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
